</given-names></name><name><surname>Cobb</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Rapley</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Killoy</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Spencer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Migration of human gingival fibroblasts over guided tissue regeneration barrier materials</article-title><source>J Periodontol</source><year>1996</year><volume>67</volume><fpage>236</fpage><lpage>244</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8708955</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pinholt</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Madsen</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Donath</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Histological evaluation of different biodegradable and non-biodegradable membranes implanted subcutaneously in rats</article-title><source>J Craniomaxillofac Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>116</fpage><lpage>122</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10958425</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>